## Why This Is Asked
This interview question explores cross-region, multi-tenant data routing with dynamic policy-driven enrichment, end-to-end observability, and integration of AWS data primitives beyond basic pipelines.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-region routing with tenant isolation
- OPA-driven enrichment at ingestion with hot policy refresh via changelog stream
- Idempotent writes to S3 Parquet and DynamoDB
- AWS Glue catalog integration with Athena for analytics
- OpenTelemetry end-to-end tracing
- Per-tenant DLQ handling and retry strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: ingestion Lambda
async function processRecord(record, ctx) {
  const tenantId = extractTenantId(record);
  const region = extractRegion(record);
  const enriched = await enrichWithOPARules(record, tenantId);
  await writeToS3Parquet(enriched, tenantId, region);
  await writeToDynamoDB(enriched, tenantId);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical ingestion patterns, per-record validation, dedupe, and multi-destination storage, plus observability.

## Key Concepts

- Kinesis Data Streams, Lambda consumption
- DynamoDB for dedupe and latest state
- S3 Parquet storage with partitioning by date and deviceType
- DLQ via SQS for invalid records
- Glue Schema Registry optional validation
- AWS X-Ray tracing and LocalStack testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Lambda handler sketch: validate, upsert, write
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  for (const record of event.Records) {
    const payload = JSON.parse(Buffer.from(record.kinesis.data, 'base64').toString());
    // validate against schema (pseudo)
    const valid = validate(payload);
    if (!valid) {
      await dlqSend(payload);
      continue;
    }
    await updateLatest(payload);
    await writeParquet(payload);
  }
};
```

